From 78fd6e80d8d0224808af52c21b555b4ba3a3f7cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 03:22:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(app): refusal ghost where a frame map or a merge
 came first

The part-way refusals #871 left owed now hand back their partial path in
the frame of the path the generator returns, so it lands where the part
is once run_job maps that frame:

- finishing3d raster/rings/swarf_multi carry the moves built so far;
  Rotary Contour/Parallel carry that ghost (and the radial relink's) out
  through the same pose law and world exit as the path (rotary::to_world)
- the 5-axis stamp's shank refusal carries the world plan before its
  move; the swarf link laws, the curve walk, the rotary C gate, the
  fixture route and the cross drill's part law carry the world path
- the cross drill's rapids/holder laws carry the spindle-frame chain
  back by the spindle shift
- nested refusals (pocket3d air split, rest ladder, stitched contour
  runs) put the outer moves in front of the inner ghost
  (GenError::after_moves / Ghost::after)

Success paths are untouched. The sites left without a ghost, with
reasons, are in docs/decisions/1015-ghost-frames.md. Face under an area
turn is handled by #1023.

Fixes #1015

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
